  "what": [
    "For each pack this file records what a small panel of models actually scored under the deployed Tier 0 v2-draft configuration, in two arms: unadapted (the model was told nothing about the pack) and adapted (the model was given the pack and its management guide first).",
    "It is a descriptive reference, not a threshold. A score report places an attempt inside or outside the unadapted range of this panel and says nothing further; no band is a pass and no band is a failure.",
    "The panel is five models measured once per cell on 2026-08-15. It is small, it is not a random sample of anything, and the run-to-run spread on a single configuration is large enough (mean |delta| 0.0649 across eight repeat pairs) that a difference smaller than roughly 0.16 should not be read as a difference at all.",
    "The adapted arm is included so an operator can run the same comparison on their own model: measure once unadapted, once after supplying the pack, and report the delta. That within-model delta is a more informative quantity than either score alone, because it does not require the two models being compared to be equally capable."
  ],
